Satisfaction assertions on an exported interface of an importable package: one of
an exported type, one of an unexported type. Nothing names the interface as a type.
A command imports the package for its effects, so an application links it.

-- go.mod --
module example.com/lib

go 1.27.0
-- lib.go --
package lib

type Published interface {
	Do()
}

type Exported struct{}

func (*Exported) Do() {}

type hidden struct{}

func (hidden) Do() {}

var _ Published = (*Exported)(nil)

var _ Published = hidden{}
-- cmd/app/main.go --
package main

import _ "example.com/lib"

func main() {}
